# and shows a LIVE example, so plain cat hides the trick and a safe tool reveals it.
# Nothing impersonates a real product or record; the file's own title/framing say
# "safe demo". Classes shown (all display/notify state only, reset-recoverable):
#   homoglyph (Cyrillic U+0430, Greek U+03BF); ASCII look-alike (rn->m, no Unicode);
#   bidi override (U+202E); zero-width (U+200B); invisible/BOM (U+FEFF); combining
#   marks (Zalgo); fullwidth forms (U+FF2x); control byte (CR + ESC[2K repaint hiding
#   FAILED behind OK); hidden-by-colour (SGR fg==bg); DEC charset shift; OSC 8
#   hyperlink (visible example.com -> target example.org); OSC 9 notification (safe
#   wording); OSC 0 title hijack; CSI ?1049h alt-screen; and honest Greek text as the
#   NON-attack contrast case. Deliberately NOT included (unsafe to fire from a file):
#   OSC 52 clipboard write and input reflection/answerback -- the board says so.
